uv run pytest
```

## Background tasks
{% if use_redis %}
Tasks are defined with `django_tasks.task()` (see `apps/{{ initial_app_name }}/tasks.py`)
and run on the RQ backend against Redis. A `worker` service in `docker-compose.yml` runs
`manage.py rqworker default --job-class django_tasks_rq.backend.Job`. In tests, the
`ImmediateBackend` runs tasks synchronously so no Redis is needed in CI.
{% else %}
Tasks are defined with `django_tasks.task()` (see `apps/{{ initial_app_name }}/tasks.py`)
and run synchronously in-process via `ImmediateBackend` — no Redis or worker process
needed. This is fine for simple apps, but it blocks the request while the task runs.
Regenerate this project with `use_redis=true` to switch to the RQ-backed async backend.
{% endif %}
This project uses `django-tasks` (the Django 6.0 `django.tasks` backport) so the
migration path to native Django 6.0 LTS task support (~April 2027) should mainly involve
an import-path swap.


